The test sets `command_token = "/Start@WrongBot"` and assigns the message a bot whose username is `"qa_bot"`. In `CommandHandler.check_update`, the code slices off the leading slash to get `command = "Start@WrongBot"`, splits that on `"@"` to get `["Start", "WrongBot"]`, and compares `command_parts[1].lower()` against `message.get_bot().username.lower()`. Lowercasing those two values gives `"wrongbot"` and `"qa_bot"`.

## Answer
{"condition_values":["wrongbot","qa_bot"]}
